to go there if the dice turn capricious on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are Unleashing then pretty much tapping into Dark Age Fae magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:20:50-07:00","id":1093206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1093125#post1093125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are Unleashing then pretty much tapping into Dark Age Fae magic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you've ever seen The Last Unicorn, Unleashing is when Schmendrick is trying to save the unicorn and he says &quot;magic, do as you will!&quot; and the magic changes her into a human. It's the perfect example of Unleashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:48:03-07:00","id":1093249,"title":"","content":"Ive seen the movie... would point out he was closer to a mage, but I think your right its about the same flair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:49:59-07:00","id":1093253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1092895#post1092895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Sidhe Child:</b> Give me cookies.<br /> <br /> <b>Parents:</b> Here sweetie, have a cookie. Want another cookie? Why aren't you eating your cookies? Take the cookie! Eat the DAMN Cookie!!! and so on, and so on......<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> was thinking something closer to forcing her to see a psychyatrist, or unduly interfering too much with her life at court... if she unleashed over <i>cookies</i>... I think her Guardian would pop in for a 'little chat'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:53:54-07:00","id":1093256,"title":"","content":"I think the depiction of the Unleashing is the point, not whether or not the character resembles a splat in a completely unrelated media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T08:02:22-07:00","id":1093259,"title":"","content":"So, trying to grok unleashing... From my understanding you have to have at least one dot in an art to unleash it, does the art you use have to reflect what you are trying to achieve... say I want my house to move across the street... do I need wayfare 1 and my house magically appears across the street in some fashion or can I use contracts and watch as my house burns down taking the house across the street with it along with lovely Mrs. Judy, whom you shared tea with every weekend. Then discover Mrs Judy left me her property and enough money to rebuild my house and refurnish exactly in her will... or well whatever weirdness....<br /> <br /> Any art? Or related art....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":".  OMG Autocorrect on my tablet hit this post HARD... sorry 05-16-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T08:28:32-07:00","id":1093269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1093259#post1093259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, trying to grok unleashing... From my understanding you have to have at least one dot in an art to unleash it, does the art you use have to reflect what you are trying to achieve... say I want my house to move across the street... do I need warfare 1 and my house Magica across in some fashion or can I use contracts and watch as my house burns down taking the house across the street with it along with lovely Mrs. Judy whomever shared tea with every weekend. Then discover Mrs Judy left me her property and enough money to rebuild my house and refurbish exactly in her will... or well whatever weirdness....<br /> <br /> Any art? Or related art....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It has to be related. Though, the spirit of Changeling is to reward creativity when using magic. If a childling doesn't want to clean her room, I could see her Unleashing Contract (make a deal with the room to be clean), Pyretics (&quot;purify&quot; the uncleanliness, with hilariously apropos side effects), or even Legerdemain (think The Sorcerer's Apprentice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:31:25-07:00","id":1093353,"title":"","content":"On using unleashing for STUPID things? <br /> <br /> how do you think a Changelings mentor will react?<br /> <br /> the Sidhe I think about most are Ailil, sorry, but it is true.<br /> <br /> On one hand, they dont mind chaos, or anarchy, on the other they <i>abhor</i> stupidity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:46:26-07:00","id":1093360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1093353#post1093353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On using unleashing for STUPID things?<br /> <br /> how do you think a Changelings mentor will react?<br /> <br /> the Sidhe I think about most are Ailil, sorry, but it is true.<br /> <br /> On one hand, they dont mind chaos, or anarchy, on the other they <i>abhor</i> stupidity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure where this is coming from considering a huge (YUUUGE?) portion of Changeling is based in childish whimsy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:12:53-07:00","id":1093927,"title":"","content":"I see your point.<br /> <br /> but house Ailil places a high priority, on being collected, and at least <i>pretending</i> to be civil<br /> <br /> Another thing on the Childling unleashing soveign to get a cookie?<br /> <br /> the book says that if you unleash successfully, you automaticly call on the Wyrd,wheither your &quot;Too successful&quot; or not...<br /> <br /> doubt any childling would go through that kind of head ache to get a cookie... <br /> <br /> it would be kind of fun to imagine... Sidhe Childling unleashes Soveregn &quot;I want you to immediately Terminate the services of that Pesky Psychyatrist!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> what will their parent Remember as the mists close in on their memories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T03:30:46-07:00","id":1104671,"title":"","content":"Rather then start a thread I figure I would ask in here, what are the limits of unleashings? Could Treasures result from a use, probably very cursed if used in desperation? Could you say make your own pocket dream Realm by unleashing oneiromancy? It sounds like unleashing can be more potent and flexible then virtually all other magics including Spheres.<br /> <br /> Could say then the creation of the Wolpinjackalope be the use of something like a large amount of Fae unleashing together? Like can chimeras reach a point before becoming true Fae when they can use arts and unleashings instead of redes?<br /> <br /> Can enchantments from unleashings be broken from wear and tear? Or say can the merfolk use a contract or metamorphosis unleashing to transform a village so they can live under the sea? How big can we get? The Anchored hope setting on the forum for instance had Nunnehi create a massive Earthquake, would this have been from multiple Nunnehi say unleashing primal or some other art that could effect the Earth, ( not many specifically but if you get playful oneiromancers could aid by plucking earthquacks from dreams, soothsayers could predict it, contract could point a broken deal with the land, naming could know the lands name, and even Autumn could represent the curse aspect.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:29:30-07:00","id":1132027,"title":"","content":"Yes Unleashing is very powerful and the rules need to be a little better defined<br /> <br /> but I think Vagueness was intended.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something I was wondering?<br /> <br /> Ideas how to describe an unleashing if the kithain doing the unleashing has a charachter to his unleashings, contrary to the Art used?<br /> <br /> A Seelie Sidhe using Autumn, or a unseelie using spring...<br /> <br /> (Both COULD happen) <br /> <br /> A boggan using Chicancery.<br /> <br /> a Redcap using Primal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:38:21-07:00","id":1134141,"title":"","content":"Because of how vague Unleashing is I've implemented a few flavor bits somewhat borrowing Mages Resonance. I've had items used to channel Unleashings also carry traces of it as well as well as create minor elements in aura or appearance. One of my players unleashed against a larger chimera and in the surge of glamour he collected a piece of dross that had the resonance of pyretics.<br /> <br /> I've also had Unleashings result in Chimeras becoming solid, even two becoming changelings kiths. Unleashing I've also have had risidual effects on the environment but those have not been noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:33:44-07:00","id":1134177,"title":"","content":"fair enough its vague like the various avatar Effects in Scion God, but should not be QUITE as impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T15:49:50-07:00","id":1134288,"title":"","content":"But there is a limit to Unleashing? Can a Changeling, whatever kith, smash a whole army with a Dragon's Ire Unleashing and saying &quot;slay my enemies&quot;? Or a Changeling with Chronnus Unleash the world back in time by just a &quot;return to yesterday&quot;? Can a Changeling make the entire world forget his (or even other people) existence with a imaginative Unleashing? Can't a Changeling just summon whatever the object that they are in a quest with a Wayfare Unleash? Like jumping the whole Lord of Rings by Unleashing and saying &quot;go in the lava of Mordor&quot;s Volcano&quot; or just Unleashing and summoning the Excalibur? Is there anything that can stop a Changeling from breaking any story with this power (like the Dreaming dont allowing a few forms of Unleashing and so on)?<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistake, all you need to do to Unleash is say the request, spend two Glamour points, roll you Glamour+Nightmare dices and, if there is at least one success, the effect, whatever it is, happens. Am I right? Is there any repercussion for trying to tamper with a too high level of power? Or is there a limitation to what they can affect (or how many, or how much, or how long)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T17:44:31-07:00","id":1134305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134288#post1134288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a limit to Unleashing? Can a Changeling, whatever kith, smash a whole army with a Dragon's Ire Unleashing and saying &quot;slay my enemies&quot;? Or a Changeling with Chronnus Unleash the world back in time by just a &quot;return to yesterday&quot;? Can a Changeling make the entire world forget his (or even other people) existence with a imaginative Unleashing? Can't a Changeling just summon whatever the object that they are in a quest with a Wayfare Unleash? Like jumping the whole Lord of Rings by Unleashing and saying &quot;go in the lava of Mordor&quot;s Volcano&quot; or just Unleashing and summoning the Excalibur? Is there anything that can stop a Changeling from breaking any story with this power (like the Dreaming dont allowing a few forms of Unleashing and so on)?<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistake, all you need to do to Unleash is say the request, spend two Glamour points, roll you Glamour+Nightmare dices and, if there is at least one success, the effect, whatever it is, happens. Am I right? Is there any repercussion for trying to tamper with a too high level of power? Or is there a limitation to what they can affect (or how many, or how much, or how long)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember if you get more succeses, then your score in the Art, you'll find it works <i>too </i>well... asking what too well means was part of why I started this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T02:46:46-07:00","id":1134412,"title":"","content":"Which should make suicidal nothing to lose Changelings very dangerous, and there have been lots of those, and we don't live in a world were people have stolen the Sun and turned all the poodles into T-rexes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T03:38:02-07:00","id":1134423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134412#post1134412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which should make suicidal nothing to lose Changelings very dangerous, and there have been lots of those, and we don't live in a world were people have stolen the Sun and turned all the poodles into T-rexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if we are? <br /> <br /> Mists just made it so we'd think that whatever the changes are - they are normal (or somewhat weird, if entirely justifiable) and always were like that.<br /> <br /> If you want to find a place, ravaged by the Unleashings, look no further, than Australia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 08-27-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T03:52:26-07:00","id":1134427,"title":"","content":"I'd say, that whatever you do with Unleashing shouldn't be extremely more powerful, than your Art. <br /> <br /> Somewhat more powerful and flexible, yes.<br /> It only can get to worldbreaking, when Changeling get too successful, but it's the Storyteller who decides on how the effects change the world and where or when they stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:03:18-07:00","id":1134452,"title":"","content":"Hmmn anymore ideas on how to handle a too successful unleashing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:25:54-07:00","id":1134457,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Art and the request. If is a &quot;freeze my enemies&quot; with Winter, the legs (or even his entire body) of the Changeling might freeze too, leaving him locked near his targets. If it is a classic &quot;slay my enemies&quot; with Dragon Ire it would hurt allies or destroy nearby stuff, but with Primal the fireball would burn the target and make anything flammable near by spontaneously explode in flames. If it is a &quot;show me the most beautiful on the land to me to marry&quot; using Contract it could show many people, or leave the target aware of him and his interests, or even redress the changeling in wedding clothes. It is very situational, and can vary a lot by how many success it goes beyond the art level. The most important thing I think is try to keep the tone of the desire and the situation (dont make it always funny nor always dangerous), and to not always make the desire effect useless or worst to the Changeling (like freezing everybody, not just the changeling, or making the &quot;slay my enemies&quot; kill the Changeling). Think what the Dream would do if he herd that desire screamed and gone overdrive.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, there is no relation between the number of success in the Unleashing and the level of the effect. One success is all that is needed to create whatever Unleashing is done. More success is, actually, worst for the changeling, cause the more success he gets, easier it is to go wrong for him.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Unleashing, but it really is the most dangerous power in the World of Darkness. Mages can't do this level of stuff without spending a lot of Quintessence and exploding in paradox afterwards, Changelings just use two glamour points and get a Nightmare point and the world curve himself to his desires.<br /> <br /> As it seems over-powerful, I suggest the following rules:<br /> <br /> *- The effect can't affect something that the target can't perceive, but can show stuff beyond their regular perception.<br /> *- The bigger the amount of (people, space, size, etc) that the effect is going to affect, the bigger the amount of success needed. If the amount is insufficient, the effect still happens, but only to the amount that it achieved. (If trying to affect a whole army, is needed 5 success, but if the Changeling only get 3, he will affect only about a parcel of them).<br /> *- The Dreaming will not allow you to jump challenges that the own Dreaming put on your way. You can't summon the object of a Quest, or to have the answer of a Riddle to enter a Trod appear to you by means of Unleashing.<br /> *- It cannot be used to do any effect that would wilfully call for a banality trigger to the Chalenging Unleashing (like destroying a treasure or killing a Fae Mortal self). The own banality building up inside of the Changeling closes the gate of the Unleash close. But of course that the Unleashed effect can get closer (like leaving the Mortal self of a Changeling badly harmed, but still alive).<br /> *- The Unleashed effects after unleashed are beyond the control of the Fae. If he invoked a &quot;Ice to froze his enemies forever&quot; but later decide to unfreeze them, he will need to find a way to unfroze them by himself (maybe another Unleash, but it would not work if it is the target of a Quest).<br /> <br /> And, to help to counter it on Fae fights, I suggest the Counter Unleash and the Banality Unleash. The first is a defensive action to use an Unleash against an Unleash. The target can use the same art to null the point of the Unleash, or be creative on the counter attack. Naturally this would be a resisted test of the Unleashings. It costs the same as a Unleash, plus a Willpower point.<br /> The second would be a way to negate a Unleash by summoning the banality on you. You gain a point of banality and have a banality trigger (so you could gain 2 points of banality) and roll your banality resisting the Unleashing, difficulty 8. You can increase the number of dices, adding your banality dots to the roll by each extra banality point your character accepts. Nothing happens in case of failure, but in case of botch the Changelings get an extra banality point and can't use arts for a scene. You can't Unleash and Banality Unleash on the same scene.<br /> <br /> What you guys think? Do you think this helps?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:30:03-07:00","id":1134612,"title":"","content":"Say Soothsay &quot;Show me the path to make my Family affluent, and rich&quot;<br /> <br /> or Soveign &quot;Make the annoying psychyatrist, kneel at my feet, then escort me out of the asylum&quot;<br /> <br /> ideas on how to twist those?<br /> <br /> it says on unleashings, that they cause everyone to see the chimerical reality...<br /> <br /> Ideas what the &quot;annoying psychyatrist&quot; will remember?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-27-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:50:50-07:00","id":1134642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134612#post1134612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say Soothsay &amp;quot;Show me the path to make my Family affluent, and rich&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With this I would say always remember that money gained is always money lost somewhere else. This alone allows for plenty of story fodder even without extra successes involved. With extra successes you might not only see the way bit twist fate and make your family suspiciously rich suspiciously fast, attracting all sort of unwanted attention not to mention the IRS. Fabulous wealth gained suddenly and through odd twists of fate can be as much a course as a blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or Soveign &amp;quot;Make the annoying psychyatrist, kneel at my feet, then escort me out of the asylum&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>With basic successes you might get exactly what you wanted. But the securityfootage of your shrink kneeling before you and escorting you out, without due papers especially, will raide a few rather banal eyebrows for sure.<br /> With extra successes this is even more disturbing as you are escorted out in a grand parade forged both of patients and staff who seem rather worshipful of you. And there just might be few low Banality folks in the mix who would remember much of it and start stalking you either as an idol to worship or a monster to destroy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it says on unleashings, that they cause everyone to see the chimerical reality...<br /> <br /> Ideas what the &amp;quot;annoying psychyatrist&amp;quot; will remember? </div> </div> </div>Decide his/her Banality and refer to the Mists table. It is likely that the shrink wont be remembering much making the whole ordeal all the more confusing. Especially if there is security footage of him/her escorting you out as if you were a Sovereign.<br /> <br /> Personally I love the Unleashing rules and the fact how they give players just enough rope to hang themselves if they try to just Unleash the hell out of every possible problem. I see the openendedness of them as a great tool for the ST, you just need to be ready to improv a lot since especially now no plan will survive player contact. Which just makes the ST's job all the more exiting. Naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:33:22-07:00","id":1134656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134642#post1134642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this I would say always remember that money gained is always money lost somewhere else. This alone allows for plenty of story fodder even without extra successes involved. With extra successes you might not only see the way bit twist fate and make your family suspiciously rich suspiciously fast, attracting all sort of unwanted attention not to mention the IRS. Fabulous wealth gained suddenly and through odd twists of fate can be as much a course as a blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> would it be any better to learn all 4 dots of Soothsay then use augury? (Though it will probaly show a slower route) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134642#post1134642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With basic successes you might get exactly what you wanted. But the securityfootage of your shrink kneeling before you and escorting you out, without due papers especially, will raide a few rather banal eyebrows for sure.<br /> With extra successes this is even more disturbing as you are escorted out in a grand parade forged both of patients and staff who seem rather worshipful of you. And there just might be few low Banality folks in the mix who would remember much of it and start stalking you either as an idol to worship or a monster to destroy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Decide his/her Banality and refer to the Mists table. It is likely that the shrink wont be remembering much making the whole ordeal all the more confusing. Especially if there is security footage of him/her escorting you out as if you were a Sovereign.<br /> <br /> Personally I love the Unleashing rules and the fact how they give players just enough rope to hang themselves if they try to just Unleash the hell out of every possible problem. I see the openendedness of them as a great tool for the ST, you just need to be ready to improv a lot since especially now no plan will survive player contact. Which just makes the ST's job all the more exiting. Naturally YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll take it over being undone anyday!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:45:48-07:00","id":1134658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134656#post1134656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take it over being undone anyday!</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! That to me is the whole point of Unleashings, they can save you from being undone, from an unescabable situation or just clean your laundry but always with the price of twisting the world and providing endless storyhooks and new troubles for you and your group to face.<br /> <br /> Instead of a dead or undone character you get a character literally at the center of a complex web of consequences and plots and more successes on the Unleashing just mean the web can be so much more complex. One Unleashing alone could provide fodder for several sessions of play and should there be need for more Unleashings, well the web can always grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:13:13-07:00","id":1134725,"title":"","content":"hmmmn what do you think the shrink would do, especialy if he saw the video footage himself, of him kneeling, then escorting his patient out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T02:50:14-07:00","id":1134792,"title":"","content":"Imagined two changeling armies, where every soldier keeps 2 glamour for when death is near to try their chances with Wyld..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:04:07-07:00","id":1137091,"title":"","content":"hmmn maybe a contested roll, to see who is able to win?:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T17:24:03-07:00","id":1142349,"title":"","content":"I am wondering about costs and all. Unleashing is expensive: 2 Glamour and 1 Nightmare die. Inanimae can ONLY Unleash, and according to C20 it's chimerical unless they make it Wyrd, but Unleashing invokes the Wyrd, so what's the case here? Will it cost them extra to change it to Wyrd, or is that covered by the fact that the Wyrd is invoked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T05:35:30-07:00","id":1142473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088528-ajudicating-unleashings?p=1134792#post1134792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagined two changeling armies, where every soldier keeps 2 glamour for when death is near to try their chances with Wyld..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see the sheer scale and clash of commands set by the multitude of unleashings creating some sort of backlash or Wylde Storm whether the majority of unleashings were successful or not. As a consequence reality might become very warped. Other types of consequences could be:<br /> <br /> Groundhog Day Effect that lasts until the battle never starts to begin with. <br /> Wylde Storm. The Wylde as Sentient.<br /> Interchanging of the Dreaming and the Dreaming<br /> A permanent Fog that steals people memories<br /> The Dreaming becoming unstable<br /> <br /> I'm sure others have more and better ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"201